# Idol authority router

`docs/spec/law.md` is the **SUPREME one-page law**. It is authoritative over
every other document and supersedes any stale projection wherever they diverge;
where C0 or a projection conflicts with `docs/spec/law.md`, that text is corrected
to match `docs/spec/law.md`.

Start every substantive session at `docs/spec/law.md`, then `AGENTS.md`, then read
`docs/spec/canonical.md` (**blind-start** — before repository code),
`docs/spec/agent.md`, and `.agents/HARNESS.md` (generated harness boot payload
from `docs/spec/harness-projection.md`). Follow the chain to
`docs/spec/constitution.md` (structured long-form expansion of `docs/spec/law.md`;
sole home of the `law.*` identities; **Idol algebra closure is §67**). `CLAUDE.md`,
`docs/spec/source.md`, `docs/spec/host.md` (host/shell/capability closure),
`docs/spec/AUTHORITY.md`, `docs/bootstrap.md`, `.agents/AGENT_CANONICAL.md`,
`.agents/AGENT_COORDINATION.md`, and `.agents/RELEASE_READINESS.md` are
projections only.

**Idol** (`idol`, `.id`, repository `idollang/idol`) is the language identity.
Semantic law lives in `docs/spec/constitution.md` (C0). Do not migrate to the
release repository until release-readiness authorization.

Run `./tools/node/dev/generate-harness`, `./tools/node/dev/orient`, and
`./tools/node/dev/doctor` before substantive work. Identify the semantic owner and bounded boundary before editing. Prefer
deletion or convergence over new mechanisms. Do not restore historical
architecture or duplicate MCP manifests, emitters, or coordination ledgers.
